   "author": "claude",
   "description": "Exploits flag-pincer-exploiter's split opening (red move-then-defend at the flag and blue attacking arrive staggered, yellow patrols centre alone, and only green guards its home) and its two all-in reflexes: flag_stolen sends all four of its units to enemy_flag instead of chasing the carrier, and captured sends all four to their_flag again on every score. A three-unit anvil (blue, green, yellow defend our_flag) plus red patrolling centre shreds its staggered raid, its lone yellow and its predictable counter-rushes when they arrive; a pair raid then steals against its lone green home guard and the carrier walks home unchased while the champion counter-rushes into the anvil. Its slow 1200t cheap pulse mostly wastes calls on weakest-regroups-at-centre, so it cannot re-plan inside this strategy's 1500t cheap / 5400t smart cadence on a 32 budget (worst case 15 cheap + 4 smart = 19 calls in the 24000-tick cap, never a hard stop). flag_stolen here is answered by a pair plus nearest chasing the carrier — never the whole squad — flag_dropped is secured by a pair at our_flag instead of a swarm, their_flag_dropped is scooped by pair plus nearest (3 units against its pair alone), we_scored instantly re-raids with a pair against the home its captured reflex just emptied while two hold our flag, and they_scored counter-runs red while the anvil re-forms."
